  <prompt>Add the respond/direct/hybrid interaction pattern as a typed FIELD on the widget registration-contract metadata (built on the FR-08 shape from task 022) — read at runtime from registration metadata, NOT authored as per-widget prose in the system prompt. Each in-scope widget declares its pattern. Remove/avoid any per-widget interaction matrix living in the system prompt.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. React/TypeScript expertise on the SpaarkeAi widget registration contract; comfortable extending a shared metadata shape consumed at multiple sites.</role>
  <goal>Each in-scope widget declares respond/direct/hybrid as registration metadata; the interaction pattern is read from that metadata and no per-widget matrix exists in the system prompt.</goal>
  <context>
    <background>FR-13 — interaction pattern as a registration field. Today the notion of how a widget responds (respond in chat / direct to a surface / hybrid) is not a first-class field; if encoded at all it would be prompt prose. This task declares respond/direct/hybrid as a typed field on the registration-contract metadata shape introduced by task 022 (widget-type ↔ context-type + Assistant-contract fields). Task 041 consumes this field to derive follow-ons deterministically; task 050 makes the contract fields required + registry-enforced. Keep it a data field, not model prose — the pattern drives deterministic follow-on element selection (FR-14), not a prompt instruction.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>the shared registration-contract metadata shape (extended by task 022 with the Assistant-contract fields)</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.AI.Widgets/src/widgets/workspace/register-workspace-widgets.ts</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.AI.Widgets/src/widgets/workspace/register-document-viewer-widget.ts</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.AI.Widgets/src/widgets/workspace/register-search-criteria-result-widget.ts</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.AI.Widgets/src/widgets/workspace/register-structured-output-stream-widget.ts</file>
      <file>src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/components/workspace/registerComposeWidget.ts</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>
  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-039" scope="how the pattern is used">The pattern is a deterministic data field driving deterministic follow-on selection — MUST NOT become a classifier or prompt instruction that the model interprets.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-047" scope="pattern semantics">The reactive interaction pattern stays distinct from the server-initiated notification spine — declaring a pattern MUST NOT introduce a push channel.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project" scope="the field">Add ONE typed field to the existing registration shape (§11 reuse-first) — MUST NOT add a parallel per-widget matrix in the system prompt.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-012" scope="shared widgets">Shared-lib widgets stay host-agnostic; the field is declared at registration, not host-injected.</constraint>
  </constraints>
  <knowledge>
    <files>
