  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Add a typed `interactionPattern: 'respond' | 'direct' | 'hybrid'` field to the registration-contract metadata shape (from task 022).</step>
    <step order="2">Declare each in-scope widget's pattern at its registration site.</step>
    <step order="3">Ensure the pattern is read from registration metadata at runtime (available to the follow-on derivation in task 041).</step>
    <step order="4">Confirm no per-widget interaction matrix is (re)introduced into the system prompt.</step>
    <step order="5">Build the shared/SpaarkeAi packages; add/extend a unit test asserting the field is read from metadata.</step>
    <step order="6">Update TASK-INDEX ✅.</step>
  </steps>
  <escalation>
    <trigger>If a widget's interaction cannot be expressed as respond/direct/hybrid without adding prompt prose or a classifier, STOP and escalate (ADR-039 bound / §5.5) rather than encoding it as model-interpreted text.</trigger>
  </escalation>
  <justification>
    <existing>No first-class interaction-pattern field exists; the registration shape (task 022) carries context-type + overview/per-item fields but not respond/direct/hybrid.</existing>
    <extension>Yes — one typed field added to the existing registration shape; declared per widget at existing sites.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Follow-on derivation (FR-14) has no deterministic signal for how a widget responds; pattern falls back to model-invented prose (the exact anti-pattern FR-13/FR-14 close).</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>
  <outputs>
    <output type="code">the extended registration-contract metadata shape (interactionPattern field)</output>
    <output type="code">the five registration sites declaring each widget's pattern</output>
    <output type="test">a unit test asserting the pattern is read from registration metadata</output>
  </outputs>
  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">The interaction pattern is read from registration metadata (typed field).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Each in-scope widget declares its respond/direct/hybrid pattern.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No per-widget interaction matrix exists in the system prompt (negative case).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The field is a deterministic data value, not a model-interpreted prompt instruction (negative case).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Shared/SpaarkeAi packages build; the metadata-read unit test passes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
  <notes>Task 041 consumes this field to derive follow-ons; task 050 makes it a required, registry-enforced field. Sequential on the registration-shape spine — coordinate with 041/050.

COMPLETED 2026-08-11. The `interactionPattern` field (typed shape + per-widget population) already existed from task 022 — task 040's job was to make it AUTHORITATIVE + SINGLE-SOURCED, not re-author it. Changes: (1) added `getWidgetInteractionPattern(type)` to `WorkspaceWidgetRegistry.ts` (+ barrel export from `Spaarke.AI.Widgets/src/index.ts`) — the ONE canonical runtime accessor task 041's follow-on derivation MUST read through, rather than each call site re-deriving/hardcoding respond/direct/hybrid per widget type; (2) reconciled `document-viewer`'s `interactionPattern` from task 022's placeholder `'hybrid'` to `'respond'` — task 026 shipped all three per-item cards (Summarize/Draft response/Draft memo) landing `'chat'`, so `'hybrid'` (which implies a mix of chat + surface landings) was stale; `'respond'` is the value that truthfully matches the shipped cards; (3) tightened `AssistantInteractionPattern`'s JSDoc (`types/shared.ts`) to state the field's INVARIANT explicitly — respond⇒all cards land chat, direct⇒no card lands chat, hybrid⇒mixed — so the field can never silently drift from its own widget's `perItemCards[].landing` again; (4) tightened `AssistantContractCard.tool`'s JSDoc to document the two legitimate forms (real ADR-039 catalog tool name for `email`; stable client-side key with no catalog backing for `document-viewer`) — reconciling task 022's "PLACEHOLDER" framing now that task 026 shipped the real behavior.

D-8 (defer-issues.md) resolution — CLAUDE.md §6.5 Path A: task 040's POML does not scope building a grounded Compose landing (D-8's "Fix required" text). Building one (threading `body.documentId` into the `compose-draft-document` Binding dispatch) is new cross-surface wiring outside a registration-metadata task and would touch BFF-adjacent dispatch code (against 040's "no BFF C#" constraint). Decided AGAINST building it here; applied the minimal honest fix instead (the `interactionPattern` correction above). D-8 marked RESOLVED-for-this-task but left OPEN in defer-issues.md for a future task to pick up the grounded-landing build.

No per-widget interaction matrix exists in the system prompt (grep-verified across `src/client` and `src/server` — zero matches for interactionPattern/respond-direct-hybrid prose outside the registration-shape files). No hardcoded interaction-pattern branching existed elsewhere in ConversationPane/EmailPerItemCards/DocumentPerItemCards to remove — those hooks already read the finer-grained per-card `landing` field from `getWidgetAssistantContract().perItemCards`, which is correct and unchanged (task 040 did not touch card-click wiring or landings, only the widget-level `interactionPattern` summary field + its accessor).

Tests: new `WorkspaceWidgetRegistry.interactionPattern.test.ts` (9 tests — accessor single-sourcing for email/document-viewer/workspace/documents-list, undefined-for-no-contract/unregistered, and the respond/direct/hybrid↔landings invariant across the FULL registry) + updated `register-document-viewer-widget.test.ts` (interactionPattern assertion flipped to 'respond' + new accessor spot-check, 7 tests total). Full `Spaarke.AI.Widgets` suite: 41 suites / 741 tests passing (regression-clean; `register-workspace-widgets.test.ts` needs `--maxWorkers=2` + `--max-old-space-size=6144` locally — pre-existing large-suite characteristic per task 022's notes, unrelated to this change). `tsc` (Spaarke.AI.Widgets) clean. SpaarkeAi `npm run build` clean (tsc-surface-gate: 0 surface-owned errors; vite build succeeded) — no SpaarkeAi runtime code changes were needed (EmailPerItemCards.tsx/DocumentPerItemCards.tsx/ConversationPane.tsx already correctly read per-card `landing`, unaffected by the widget-level field's correction).</notes>
